# Redux — Waitlist Website Context

## What This Project Is
This is the public-facing waitlist/marketing website for Redux, an AI-powered browser-based photo editing platform. It is a standalone Next.js site that will eventually live alongside or be merged with the main Redux application. The primary goal of this site is to capture waitlist emails before the app launches.

---

## Brand

Product name: Redux
Logo: White R icon (`public/redux-logo.png`), 32×32px in Navbar and Footer — not a text wordmark
Tagline: Organize, edit, and export photos—all from your browser
Hero headline: Your AI agent for professional photo editing

Colors:
- Main background: #111111
- Primary/CTA buttons: `BTN_PRIMARY_SOLID` from `lib/button-styles.ts` — bg `#8758ed`, hover `#9a6ff2`, border `border-white/20`
- Primary button shadows: `shadow-btn-primary*` tokens in `globals.css`
- Accent gradient (progress etc.): `#682FBF` → `#8B44E8`
- Legacy brand purple (non-button accents): #794ade
- Surface (cards): #1a1a1a
- Surface 2 (nested panels): #222222
- Border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)

Fonts:
- Display/headings: SF Pro Display, CSS var --font-display
- Body: SF Pro Text, CSS var --font-body
- Fallback stack: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, system-ui, sans-serif
- Loaded via system font stack in globals.css (self-host with next/font/local when .woff2 files are added to public/fonts/)

---

## Tech Stack

- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router, TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS + CSS variables in globals.css
- Animations: Framer Motion
- Icons: lucide-react
- Components: shadcn/ui (Radix primitives)
- Fonts: SF Pro (system font stack; next/font/local when self-hosted)
- Database: Prisma ORM + PostgreSQL (Neon) — same DB as the main app
- Analytics: PostHog, Vercel Analytics
- Error tracking: Sentry
- Hosting: Vercel

